course: dictionary
lesson: 2325
title: One word, many meanings: crow
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Crow is a good example: it can be a bird, or a verb about a rooster's call, or a way of bragging. To find the right meaning, read the words around it and ask which meaning fits.
explain: «Crows gather in winter roosts and peregrines hunt pigeons from the cathedral tower.» Here crows are animals, because they gather in roosts and a bird can roost. Crow is a noun in this sentence, a large black bird.
explain: A verb tells you what someone or something does. To crow can mean a rooster making its loud morning cry, or a person boasting happily about winning. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check: if it still makes sense, you have chosen well.
explain: «As the crow flies» is an idiom, a set phrase with its own meaning. It means in a straight line, not by the winding road. When a phrase seems odd word by word, think about what the whole group of words means together.
fact: A crow is a large black bird with a loud, harsh call.
fact: To crow, said of a rooster, means to make its loud morning cry.
fact: To crow means to boast happily about winning.
fact: «As the crow flies» means in a straight line, the shortest way from one place to another.
fact: The past tense of crow is crowed, though the old form crew is also used.
exercise: «Crows gather in winter roosts and peregrines hunt pigeons from the cathedral tower.» In this sentence, what is a crow? | A boast about winning | A straight line | A rooster's morning cry | *A large black bird
exercise: The team crowed after winning the cup. What does crowed mean here? | *Boasted happily about winning | Made a loud morning cry | Hopped round the crumbs | Flew in a straight line
exercise: The school is 2 km away «as the crow flies». What does this mean? | Along the bendy road | In the dark | By the fastest bus | *In a straight line
test: In La Fontaine's fable, which animal tricks Mr Crow into dropping his cheese? | *A fox | A gull | A rat | A raccoon
test: Which bird in the example sentences gathers in winter roosts? | Sparrows | Swifts | *Crows | Blackbirds
exam: In «Pigeons and crows walk and leave one print after another», what does crows mean? | A rooster's morning cry | A straight line | *Large black birds | To boast happily about winning
